# The repository takes a whitelist approach (see /.gitignore): nothing is tracked
# until a rule allows it. /misc is the exception -- it is allowed wholesale, and
# blacklists from here instead.
#
# Why: everywhere else the set of legitimate file types is small and fixed, so a
# whitelist is short and stays short. Here it is open-ended (.tex, .sty, .bib,
# .pdf, Makefile, latexmkrc, images, ...) and grows with every document added,
# while the set of *junk* is finite and known -- LaTeX writes its build files
# next to the sources, and misc/ is the only tree where any tool does that. So
# the short list is the one below, and it is the one worth maintaining.
#
# Keep in step with clean.sh, which deletes exactly this set.
*.acn
*.aux
*.bbl
*-blx.bib
*.bcf
*.blg
*.dvi
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
*.glo
*.ist
*.loa
*.lof
*.log
*.lot
*.nav
*.out
*.run.xml
*.snm
*.synctex.gz
*.toc
*.vrb
